{#
	Video placeholder (used by the card component, `units/card/card.njk`)
	=====================================================================
	Reads `component.data.video`, set in the card's front matter. Two kinds of video:

	1. Embedded (YouTube, or any other provider in `lib/shortcodes/videoFacade.js`):
	     video:
	       provider: youtube
	       id: nsekqm6eaD8
	       title: Video title
	       start: 144          <- optional, in seconds
	   Uses the `video` shortcode, so it gets the click-to-load facade: nothing is requested from the
	   provider until play is pressed. The shortcode outputs its own 16:9 box and privacy caption.

	2. Self-hosted:
	     video:
	       custom:
	         src: { webm: /assets/videos/clip.webm, mp4: /assets/videos/clip.mp4 }
	         poster: /assets/videos/clip-poster.jpg
	         captions: /assets/videos/clip-en.vtt   <- optional, but needed if the video has speech
	         width: 1280       <- optional, defaults to 1280x720
	         height: 720
	   A plain `<video>` needs no facade: there's no third party, and the controls are the browser's own.
	   - `preload="none"` downloads nothing but the poster until play is pressed.
	   - `loading="lazy"` also defers the poster until the video is near the viewport, in browsers that
	     support it (Chrome and Edge 150 so far). Others ignore it and still get `preload="none"`.
	     Remove it for a video near the top of the page.
	   - `width` and `height` are required with `loading="lazy"`: an unloaded video is otherwise
	     300x150 and may never be seen as "near the viewport".

	NOTE: `{% video %}` is an async shortcode, and Nunjucks silently drops its output in two places:
	- inside a `{% for %}` loop: use `{% asyncEach %}` instead (as `collections/featured.njk` does)
	- in an include inside `{% if %}` or `{% elif %}`: use a separate `{% ifAsync %}` block instead
	  (as `units/card/card.njk` does). An `elif` drops it even after `ifAsync`.
#}
{% set video = component.data.video %}
{% if video.provider %}
{% video video.provider, video.id, video.title, video.start %}
{% elif video.custom %}
{# No wrapper needed: `width` and `height` give the video its shape, and the reset (`base/_reset.scss`) lets it shrink to fit #}
<video controls preload="none" loading="lazy"
	width="{{ video.custom.width | default(1280) }}" height="{{ video.custom.height | default(720) }}"
	{%- if video.custom.poster %} poster="{{ video.custom.poster }}"{% endif %}>
	{% if video.custom.src.webm %}<source src="{{ video.custom.src.webm }}" type="video/webm">{% endif %}
	{% if video.custom.src.mp4 %}<source src="{{ video.custom.src.mp4 }}" type="video/mp4">{% endif %}
	{% if video.custom.captions %}<track src="{{ video.custom.captions }}" kind="captions" srclang="en" label="English">{% endif %}
	<p>Your browser can't play this video. Here's a <a href="{{ video.custom.src.mp4 or video.custom.src.webm }}">link to the video file</a> instead.</p>
</video>
{% endif %}
